# Chrome Mox: "{T}: Add one mana of any of the exiled card's colors." Bot1 imprints Dack Fayden ({1}{U}{R}, a blue and
# red card) on turn 1 and taps the Mox for red to cast a Lightning Bolt at Bot2; a green mana is not on offer (refused
# while red is, the positive control). On turn 3 the same Mox taps for blue, the other color of the card: it is "any" of
# the colors, not the first of them.

[Bot1 Deck]
Chrome Mox
Dack Fayden
Lightning Bolt
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Chrome Mox.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Dack Fayden)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Chrome Mox.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Chrome Mox.Activate(Color: Red)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Chrome Mox.Activate(Color: Blue)
? Bot1.Mana = {U}
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Dack Fayden
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Lightning Bolt
